WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:10.846
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Alright, good morning everyone. Thanks for making the time. Let’s do a quick round of updates before we get into the policy stuff.</v>

00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:18.864
<v Kwame Asante>Morning! Not much from me, just wrapping up the onboarding checklist refresh. Should be done by Friday.</v>

00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:28.959
<v Hannah Weiss>Hey all. I’m still working through the July absence reports, but nothing major to flag. Oh, and the new leave tracker is live.</v>

00:00:29.847 --> 00:00:39.077
<v Tomás Rivera>Hi everyone. Legal’s been quiet, just a couple of contract reviews. I’ll be on PTO next week, but reachable if anything urgent pops up.</v>

00:00:40.146 --> 00:00:50.146
<v Grace Liu>Morning! I had a few check-ins with managers about the new performance templates. Feedback’s mostly positive, but a few folks are confused about the calibration process.</v>

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:57.220
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Thanks, Grace. Let’s circle back on calibration later this month. Anything else before we jump in?</v>

00:00:58.632 --> 00:01:00.170
<v Kwame Asante>Nope, all good here.</v>

00:01:00.505 --> 00:01:02.043
<v Hannah Weiss>Ready when you are.</v>

00:01:03.385 --> 00:01:10.308
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Okay, main agenda: the Talent Assessment policy page. You all saw the proposed update in the doc, right?</v>

00:01:10.852 --> 00:01:17.390
<v Grace Liu>Yep, I read through it. The new language about the FY27 Check-In cycle makes sense to me.</v>

00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:25.285
<v Tomás Rivera>Same here. I appreciate the note about France and Germany—good to call out the works council requirements.</v>

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:35.681
<v Hannah Weiss>I like that it points people to The Loop for the latest info. That should cut down on the confusion we had last year.</v>

00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:42.622
<v Kwame Asante>Yeah, I think it’s clearer. Just to confirm, we’re keeping the navigation links at the bottom, right?</v>

00:01:43.188 --> 00:01:53.188
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Yes, we’ll keep those. The idea is to add the review notice at the top, then the redirect to The Loop, and then the existing navigation.</v>

00:01:53.662 --> 00:02:00.200
<v Grace Liu>Quick question—should we mention anywhere that the Netherlands council already approved? Or is that too much detail?</v>

00:02:00.846 --> 00:02:05.846
<v Tomás Rivera>I’d keep it. It’s helpful context, especially since people ask about country differences.</v>

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:18.094
<v Hannah Weiss>Agreed. I think it’s fine as is. The only thing I’m wondering is, do we need to specify a timeline for when France and Germany might get a decision?</v>

00:02:19.402 --> 00:02:27.479
<v Sofia Lindqvist>We don’t have a firm date yet, so I’d rather not commit to anything. We can update once we know more.</v>

00:02:28.336 --> 00:02:35.259
<v Kwame Asante>Makes sense. I’ll just leave it as 'no final decisions will be made until those processes are complete.'</v>

00:02:35.786 --> 00:02:37.324
<v Grace Liu>Sounds good to me.</v>

00:02:38.705 --> 00:02:40.243
<v Tomás Rivera>No objections from Legal.</v>

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:42.010
<v Hannah Weiss>All good here.</v>

00:02:43.034 --> 00:02:56.111
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Alright, so we’re agreed: we’ll update the Talent Assessment page with the new review notice, the redirect to The Loop, and the country-specific note. Kwame, can you take the action to update the handbook?</v>

00:02:57.389 --> 00:03:01.620
<v Kwame Asante>Yep, I’ll get that done. Should I aim for the 18th?</v>

00:03:01.877 --> 00:03:07.262
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Yes, let’s set the deadline for August 18th. Ping me if you need anything.</v>

00:03:07.895 --> 00:03:09.395
<v Kwame Asante>Will do.</v>

00:03:09.766 --> 00:03:11.266
<v Grace Liu>Thanks, Kwame.</v>

00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:14.239
<v Tomás Rivera>Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:03:14.649 --> 00:03:16.149
<v Hannah Weiss>Thanks!</v>

00:03:16.924 --> 00:03:22.693
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Okay, last thing—quick note on the engagement survey. We got the preliminary results back yesterday.</v>

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.349
<v Grace Liu>Oh, nice. Anything surprising?</v>

00:03:26.278 --> 00:03:32.816
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Not really—participation was up, which is great. But there’s still some confusion about the new benefits portal.</v>

00:03:33.162 --> 00:03:38.162
<v Kwame Asante>Yeah, I’ve had a few people ping me about where to find stuff.</v>

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:44.206
<v Hannah Weiss>Same here. Maybe we need a quick FAQ or a Loom walkthrough?</v>

00:03:45.304 --> 00:03:52.996
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Good idea. Kwame, can you draft a short FAQ for the benefits portal? Just the top five questions or so.</v>

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:56.467
<v Kwame Asante>Sure thing. I’ll get that started this week.</v>

00:03:56.714 --> 00:04:00.560
<v Grace Liu>Let me know if you want input on the questions.</v>

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.779
<v Kwame Asante>Will do, thanks Grace.</v>

00:04:03.697 --> 00:04:08.312
<v Tomás Rivera>If you need Legal to review anything, just send it my way.</v>

00:04:09.071 --> 00:04:10.571
<v Kwame Asante>Thanks, Tomás.</v>

00:04:10.825 --> 00:04:13.902
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Alright, I think that’s everything. Any other business?</v>

00:04:14.576 --> 00:04:16.076
<v Hannah Weiss>Nothing from me.</v>

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:18.989
<v Grace Liu>All good here.</v>

00:04:20.453 --> 00:04:21.953
<v Tomás Rivera>I’m set.</v>

00:04:22.205 --> 00:04:23.705
<v Kwame Asante>I’m good.</v>

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:32.063
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Great. Thanks, everyone. I’ll send out the notes and action items after this. Have a good rest of your day!</v>

00:04:33.149 --> 00:04:34.649
<v Grace Liu>You too!</v>

00:04:35.716 --> 00:04:37.216
<v Hannah Weiss>Bye all.</v>

00:04:37.876 --> 00:04:39.376
<v Tomás Rivera>Take care.</v>

00:04:40.304 --> 00:04:41.804
<v Kwame Asante>See you.</v>

00:04:43.141 --> 00:04:44.641
<v Sofia Lindqvist>Meeting adjourned.</v>
